! mcp_bootstrap_p46.strap -- THE BREAKDOWN ROUTINE's re-entry, its
! save area and its tables, printed page 46.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.53, header "PAGE NUMBER 46".
! docs/boot_plan.md M3.
!
! >>> THIS PAGE DEFINES EVERY ONE OF printed p.45's FOURTEEN
! STAND-INS, AND NOT ONE OF THEM MOVES. <<<
!
!   QX INN  $1          line 22    QX OUT  $2          line 23
!   QX CF9  $3          line 24    Q KSIZ  6           line 33
!   QW CF9  002555.00   line 28    Q SKIP  002556.00   line 29
!   Q CMA   002556.31   line 30    QCOUNT  002556.37   line 31
!   Q BLNK  002556.61   line 32
!   Q SAV1  002547.00   line 16    Q SAV2  002550.00   line 17
!   Q SAV3  002551.00   line 18    Q SAV4  002552.00   line 19
!   Q SAV6  002554.00   line 21
!
! AND THE TWO dds p.45 HAD TO WRITE BY HAND ARE PRINTED HERE: lines
! 30 and 32 are "(A*)DD(BU,Q KSIZ,Q KSIZ)", which is (BU,6,6) --
! exactly what p.45's stand-ins carried, and what its lines 20 and 22
! print as 006600 without writing any dds of their own.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THREE MORE SWAPs, AND NOW THERE ARE NINE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 2-4 are "Q BRK8  SWAPI,1,QX INN,Q SAV1" and its two fellows,
! under line 1's comment "-RE-ENTRY POINT FOLLOWING ERROR RETURN".
! They are the mirror of printed p.45 lines 47-49: p.45 swapped the
! live index registers into Q SAV on the way OUT of the error, and
! these swap them back on the way IN.  Line 5's "TI,2,Q SAV4,$L" is
! likewise p.45 line 50's "TI,2,$L,Q SAV4" reversed.
!
! So the instruction the model refuses has NINE documented callers:
! two on printed p.40, one on p.43, three on p.45, three here.  The
! run executes none of them -- tests/gen_tb.py's op_trail measures
! that -- and the refusal survives with an expiry date.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! AND THE PAGE CORRECTED THE ASSEMBLER IN FOUR PLACES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) VF IS TWENTY-FIVE BITS AND THE NEXT FIELD STARTS AT BIT 25.
!     C22-6531 printed p.18 says "THE LOCATION COUNTER STANDS AT BIT
!     25 at the end of the operation", and strap_asm.py had carried a
!     note saying so while returning a whole half word anyway,
!     because "nothing in the corpus distinguishes the two".  LINES
!     29 AND 30 DO: "Q SKIP  VF,.16" is at 002556.00 and the very
!     next row, "Q CMA  (A*)DD(...)", is at 002556.31 -- bit 25.
!
!     The ALIGNMENT stays a half word, which is the whole trick: p.18
!     rounds the counter up BEFORE compiling the value, so a run of
!     VFs still measures in half words and only a following
!     pseudo-operation that does not round sees bit 25.
!
! (b) A NULL OPERATION ALIGNS TO A HALF WORD.  It did not, which was
!     invisible until (a): printed p.25 lines 41-42 are a "VF,4.0"
!     and a ",0.0($7)" on consecutive rows, and the half word would
!     have started at bit 25 and overlapped the VF.
!
! (c) A CONSTANT SYN IS RESOLVED BEFORE THE LOCATION WALK.  Lines 30
!     and 32 write "(BU,Q KSIZ,Q KSIZ)" and line 33 -- THREE ROWS
!     BELOW -- defines it.  The location counter needs those lengths
!     to walk past them.  C22-6531 printed p.31 allows the forward
!     reference outright: a SYN's operand need only be "fully defined
!     (although this may possibly mean as late as pass 3 of Strap-1)".
!
! (d) A DATA SYMBOL CARRIES ITS dds, which is the other end of the
!     same p.31 sentence printed p.45 needed.  Line 30 defines Q CMA
!     with (BU,Q KSIZ,Q KSIZ); p.45 line 20's bare "KF,Q CMA" prints
!     006600 and p.46's own line 9 is the same row.
!
! AND (a) FOUND A MISSING LINE IN ANOTHER DECK.  printed p.8 line 31
! is "X E DD K  SYN,$-X ERR DD" and prints 000047.00, a whole word,
! which a 25-bit VF would make 000046.71.  LINE 30 OF THAT PAGE IS A
! "CNOP" and mcp_bootstrap_p7_p8.strap had omitted it -- invisible
! while VF claimed a half word, and the first thing to fail when it
! stopped.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.
!
! (2) NOTHING ELSE.  "XW," with a null value field is written as
!     printed and compiles as a zero (C22-6531 printed p.7: "A null
!     field is always compiled as a zero"); line 20's "XW" with no
!     comma at all is written the same way.  The comma and the blank
!     on lines 30 and 32 are written as the listing writes them,
!     ",,*" and ", *".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE TWO STAND-INS THIS PAGE NEEDS, both on printed p.45
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   Q NEXT  002507.40   line 11's BAE target
!   Q RSTR  002526.00   line 8's CBZ target

        SLC, (8)2536.0

QNEXT   SYN, (8)2507.40
QRSTR   SYN, (8)2526.0

        SLC, (8)2536.0

! ---- the re-entry: swap the saved indexes back ---------------------
QBRK8   SWAPI, 1, QXINN, QSAV1      ! line 2  -RESET INDEXES
        SWAPI, 1, QXOUT, QSAV2      ! line 3
        SWAPI, 1, QXCF9, QSAV3      ! line 4
        TI, 2, QSAV4, $L            ! line 5  -RESET $L AND $R
        LX, $15, QSAV6              ! line 6
        V+, QXOUT, QSKIP            ! line 7  -SKIP TO BEG OF NEXT
                                     !           OUTPUT FIELD

! ---- skip blanks until the next comma ------------------------------
QSPAC   CBZ, QXINN, QRSTR           ! line 8  -TEST FOR LAST INPUT
                                     !           CHAR
        KF, QCMA                    ! line 9  -TEST FOR COMMA.  FIRST
                                     ! line 10   CANNOT BE A COMMA
        BAE, QNEXT                  ! line 11
        LF(V+I)(BU,QKSIZ), QKSIZ(QXINN)   ! line 12 -LOAD NEXT INPUT
                                           !           CHAR
        B, QSPAC                    ! line 13

! ---- the save area --------------------------------------------------
QSAV1   XW,                         ! line 16 -STORE INDEXES
QSAV2   XW,                         ! line 17
QSAV3   XW,                         ! line 18
QSAV4   XW,                         ! line 19 -STORE $L
        XW                          ! line 20 -STORE $R
QSAV6   XW,                         ! line 21 -STORE $15

QXINN   SYN, $1                     ! line 22
QXOUT   SYN, $2                     ! line 23
QXCF9   SYN, $3                     ! line 24

! ---- PROGRAM MODIFICATION CARDS, lines 25-27's banner ---------------
QWCF9   XW, 0., 9, QWCF9            ! line 28 -NO. OF CHARS PER
                                     !           OUTPUT FIELD
QSKIP   VF, .16                     ! line 29 -NO. OF BIT BETWEEN
                                     !           SUCCESSIVE FIELDS
QCMA    (A*)DD(BU,QKSIZ,QKSIZ),,*    ! line 30 -COMMA
QCOUNT  DD(BU,18), (8)000014        ! line 31 -MAX. NO. FIELDS
QBLNK   (A*)DD(BU,QKSIZ,QKSIZ), *    ! line 32 -BLANK
QKSIZ   SYN, 6                      ! line 33

        END, QBRK8

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! AND ONE LISTING MARK, the bare "*" after the location that every
! page since printed p.3 carries: line 9 ("002543.40 *").
